  "worked_solution": "To compute $P(B|A),$ we need to ask, \"what is the probability of $B$ occurring given that $A$ has occurred?\"\n\nSince we are assuming that $A$ has occurred, we only consider the events inside $A.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14273146/assets/56a6299b9db053fe3ab235c2cc98f7dfdb849beb37d3f2987026a6f89aa4191b.png)\n\nThe probability of event $A$ occurring is\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.2+0.05=0.25.\n$$\n\nNow, $P(B|A)$ can be interpreted as the proportion of $B$ that lies inside $A,$ relative to the size of $A.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(B|A)=\\frac{0.05}{0.25}=0.2.\n$$",
